WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.283 --> 00:00:05.743
- Good morning, Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.743 --> 00:00:07.710
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.369
that entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:10.981
of the major problems in the world.

00:00:10.981 --> 00:00:12.222
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:15.226
today we're going to talk
about how you can stay calm

00:00:15.226 --> 00:00:17.248
in stressful situations.

00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:19.103
Rule number four is my personal favorite,

00:00:19.103 --> 00:00:21.973
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:21.973 --> 00:00:23.317
And as always as you're watching

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.404
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:25.404 --> 00:00:27.163
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:29.587
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:31.126
You might win a prize, too.

00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:32.581
And also, when you write it down,

00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:35.805
it's much more likely to
stick to yourself as well.

00:00:35.805 --> 00:00:37.135
Enjoy!

00:00:37.135 --> 00:00:39.718
(upbeat music)

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.641
- I know, without a question,

00:00:56.641 --> 00:00:58.316
that one of the most important
decisions you will make

00:00:58.316 --> 00:01:02.298
in your entire lifetime is
to better handle stress.

00:01:02.298 --> 00:01:04.877
To decide that your identity
and who you are anymore,

00:01:04.877 --> 00:01:05.753
you're not going to be as stressed

00:01:05.753 --> 00:01:08.139
as you were last year or the year before.

00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:11.944
We should all become more
peaceful, more thoughtful,

00:01:11.944 --> 00:01:15.841
more present, more
joyous people as we age,

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.195
would you not agree?

00:01:17.195 --> 00:01:21.195
And if that's true, then
it's time to start now.

00:01:24.761 --> 00:01:26.386
- Rule number one is have a schedule.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:29.131
One of the things that
really helped me stay calm

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:31.181
with all the things that were
happening with my business

00:01:31.181 --> 00:01:32.332
was to have a schedule.

00:01:32.332 --> 00:01:33.962
And I know that there's a time

00:01:33.962 --> 00:01:36.739
for the thing that is causing an issue.

00:01:36.739 --> 00:01:39.261
And so, for example,
Tuesday is my YouTube day.

00:01:39.261 --> 00:01:41.442
It's when I review all
the videos from my team,

00:01:41.442 --> 00:01:42.545
it's when I answer any questions,

00:01:42.545 --> 00:01:44.235
when I do set ups for collaborations,

00:01:44.235 --> 00:01:45.221
when I'm doing the research,

00:01:45.221 --> 00:01:48.375
anything basically YouTube
related except for filming,

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:49.648
I do on a Tuesday.

00:01:49.648 --> 00:01:52.627
And so whenever I get
e-mails during the week,

00:01:52.627 --> 00:01:55.722
I get questions, I get
proposals, I get ideas,

00:01:55.722 --> 00:01:59.204
I review a video that then
spawns another creation,

00:01:59.204 --> 00:02:01.705
I have a place, I put it in my folder,

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:03.613
and I know on Tuesday
I'm going to have time

00:02:03.613 --> 00:02:04.571
to go out and do it.

00:02:04.571 --> 00:02:06.651
And I think often times when we don't

00:02:06.651 --> 00:02:07.644
have time to figure it out,

00:02:07.644 --> 00:02:09.963
and we try to rush to
solve it, it creates chaos,

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.108
it creates stress, but
knowing that you have a place

00:02:12.108 --> 00:02:14.754
in your calendar to be able to do it.

00:02:14.754 --> 00:02:16.956
For me at least, it creates
a great sense of calm.

00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:18.177
- When I have a difficult day

00:02:18.177 --> 00:02:19.793
here's one of the first things that I do.

00:02:19.793 --> 00:02:21.594
I will get on my mountain bike,

00:02:21.594 --> 00:02:25.670
and I will ride like
a bat out of wherever,

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:30.124
through the forest, and that
releases dopamine in my brain

00:02:30.124 --> 00:02:33.445
which is the neurotransmitter
of inspiration.

00:02:33.445 --> 00:02:36.882
And that releases serotonin,
moving, right, on the bicycle.

00:02:36.882 --> 00:02:38.549
It releases serotonin

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:41.448
which is the pleasure neurotransmitter.

00:02:41.448 --> 00:02:45.649
And it cuts down on my cortisol
which is the fear hormone.

00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:48.630
So just simply going for
a mountain bike ride,

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.861
or going for a swim, or
getting into yoga class,

00:02:51.861 --> 00:02:53.748
or something as simple
as going for a walk,

00:02:53.748 --> 00:02:58.562
or maybe even doing jumping
jacks when no one is looking

00:02:58.562 --> 00:03:02.288
will create a pharmacy of
mastery within your brain

00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:04.409
which will affect your psychology,

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:07.753
your neurobiology, and your interior life,

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.189
which makes you just feel a lot better.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.202
You know that, after a work
out you always feel different

00:03:12.202 --> 00:03:14.615
than you did before you
went into the work out.

00:03:14.615 --> 00:03:16.725
And related to a pharmacy of mastery,

00:03:16.725 --> 00:03:20.744
it's something that I
have counted on for years.

00:03:20.744 --> 00:03:22.032
When I've had good seasons,

00:03:22.032 --> 00:03:25.542
when I've had challenging
seasons of my life, massage.

00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:27.597
I call it the two massage protocol.

00:03:27.597 --> 00:03:32.002
Two massages every single
week, it moves your lymph,

00:03:32.002 --> 00:03:35.336
it moves your blood which
oxygenates your system,

00:03:35.336 --> 00:03:38.744
it reduces toxicity, you
feel a whole lot better.

00:03:38.744 --> 00:03:39.577
- You know what?

00:03:39.577 --> 00:03:41.024
There has to be an intentional decision

00:03:41.024 --> 00:03:42.336
at some point in our lives where we say,

00:03:42.336 --> 00:03:45.094
"Look, I'm not going to
be this stressed anymore.

00:03:45.094 --> 00:03:48.366
"I'm allowing too much
stress into my life."

00:03:48.366 --> 00:03:50.207
And please notice the
words I'm using here,

00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:54.093
I'm allowing too much stress into my life.

00:03:54.093 --> 00:03:56.570
Most stress is not, quote unquote, real.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.725
No one hands you a plate of stress,

00:03:58.725 --> 00:04:01.718
it's not something you see and
we can transact and exchange.

00:04:01.718 --> 00:04:04.364
It's something we make up in our mind.

00:04:04.364 --> 00:04:08.127
We make things stressful
that may or may not be

00:04:08.127 --> 00:04:11.618
or have any cause to be stress inducing.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.539
You know, one thing that
could stress you out

00:04:13.539 --> 00:04:16.346
might not be a stressful
thing to anybody else.

00:04:16.346 --> 00:04:18.518
So that proves we're making it up.

00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:19.648
And since we're making it up,

00:04:19.648 --> 00:04:22.844
we should decide what we're
going to do in the future.

00:04:22.844 --> 00:04:25.853
Are we going to be always be
these stressful people or not?

00:04:25.853 --> 00:04:27.966
I know that sounds so silly
but I made that decision

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:30.769
when I was young, I was
20 years old, and I said,

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.809
"Look, I don't want to be a
stressful person anymore."

00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:36.018
I used to stress about
getting everything right,

00:04:36.018 --> 00:04:37.152
and getting good grades.

00:04:37.152 --> 00:04:40.795
I'd stress about pleasing
people and stress about,

00:04:40.795 --> 00:04:42.907
did I fit in, I'd stress about college,

00:04:42.907 --> 00:04:44.568
I'd stress about, and
at some point I said,

00:04:44.568 --> 00:04:46.764
"All this is made up."

00:04:46.764 --> 00:04:49.681
You know, matter of fact,
most stress is coming from,

00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:51.580
usually, one of two things.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.042
First is a false time
crunch that we perceive.

00:04:56.042 --> 00:04:57.322
We think we only have so much time,

00:04:57.322 --> 00:04:58.477
so everything becomes stressful,

00:04:58.477 --> 00:04:59.789
"Oh my God, I got to get this
done, I got to get this done.

00:04:59.789 --> 00:05:00.818
"I got to get this done."

00:05:00.818 --> 00:05:05.009
And we're reacting our lives
to really false deadlines.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:06.296
Someone asks you for something,

00:05:06.296 --> 00:05:08.791
you think you have to get
it to them right away.

00:05:08.791 --> 00:05:09.874
You probably don't.

00:05:09.874 --> 00:05:13.078
It's probably not a real
deadline, and unless you ask them,

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:15.622
"When is the real deadline on this?"

00:05:15.622 --> 00:05:18.840
I mean the point in
which everything crumbles

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.673
and falls apart.

00:05:19.673 --> 00:05:23.074
If you don't get it
then, what would happen?

00:05:23.074 --> 00:05:24.167
What is the worst thing that would happen

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.888
if you didn't get it at that exact time?

00:05:25.888 --> 00:05:27.495
I'm crazy about this in my life.

00:05:27.495 --> 00:05:29.384
If someone says, "Well Brendan,
I need this by Thursday,"

00:05:29.384 --> 00:05:31.993
I say, "Okay, if you need it by Thursday,

00:05:31.993 --> 00:05:33.608
"is Thursday the day that everything

00:05:33.608 --> 00:05:36.193
"would explode and fall
apart if you didn't get it?"

00:05:36.193 --> 00:05:40.001
And they're like, "No, I mean,
no, Monday would be fine."

00:05:40.001 --> 00:05:42.521
And I just bought myself
Thursday, Friday, Saturday,

00:05:42.521 --> 00:05:44.164
Sunday, and part of the day Monday.

00:05:44.164 --> 00:05:47.293
I just bought five days by asking

00:05:47.293 --> 00:05:48.566
when the real deadline is,

00:05:48.566 --> 00:05:52.034
'cause most people, they say
they want something from you,

00:05:52.034 --> 00:05:54.981
when they want it, not when they need it.

00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:57.989
So your job, to help deal
with just the time crunch

00:05:57.989 --> 00:06:00.851
that stress can feel like, is asking,

00:06:00.851 --> 00:06:02.983
"When is the real deadline?"

00:06:02.983 --> 00:06:05.663
And all these things that
you're stressed out about,

00:06:05.663 --> 00:06:07.619
do they really need to
be handled right now,

00:06:07.619 --> 00:06:09.151
this immediate second?

00:06:09.151 --> 00:06:11.110
Would it be okay if you created a plan

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:13.194
and you handle them over
the next couple of days,

00:06:13.194 --> 00:06:16.251
next couple of weeks,
next couple of months?

00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:19.855
When you actually realize the
unbelievable amount of time

00:06:19.855 --> 00:06:24.276
we all have as humans, and
how much more time we have

00:06:24.276 --> 00:06:29.020
when we become focused, diligent,
intentional, disciplined,

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.537
then we're not so much stressed anymore.

00:06:30.537 --> 00:06:32.634
It's like, I will get
to that, when the time

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:33.998
is appropriate for that.

00:06:33.998 --> 00:06:36.230
Before that, I've got other things.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.181
- Now you've got a sort of five point plan

00:06:38.181 --> 00:06:40.926
that anyone can follow to get over stress

00:06:40.926 --> 00:06:42.212
and trauma in their lives.

00:06:42.212 --> 00:06:43.045
Talk me through it.

00:06:43.045 --> 00:06:45.001
- Well I think, first of all I
want to make one thing clear.

00:06:45.001 --> 00:06:46.349
The quality of your life is the quality

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:47.548
of where you live emotionally.

00:06:47.548 --> 00:06:48.857
We all have a home.

00:06:48.857 --> 00:06:50.554
Angry people find a way to get angry

00:06:50.554 --> 00:06:52.420
even if their life doesn't give
anything to be angry about,

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.253
we can always find it.

00:06:53.253 --> 00:06:54.410
Sad people can find a way to be sad.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.550
Caring people find a way
to care for other people.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.599
So one thing you need to identify
is, where are you living?

00:06:58.599 --> 00:07:00.340
What's your home, what's your habit?

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.766
And then the way to change it is,

00:07:01.766 --> 00:07:03.261
when I was homeless literally on my own,

00:07:03.261 --> 00:07:05.114
just getting started, I
didn't have the internet

00:07:05.114 --> 00:07:06.745
but I decided I had to go to a library

00:07:06.745 --> 00:07:08.073
and I had to feed my mind.

00:07:08.073 --> 00:07:10.566
And I always tell people
the first stage is,

00:07:10.566 --> 00:07:12.122
you know, weeds grow automatically.

00:07:12.122 --> 00:07:13.547
One of my teachers taught me, he said,

00:07:13.547 --> 00:07:15.245
"Every day stand guard
of the door of your mind

00:07:15.245 --> 00:07:16.449
"and feed it something good,"

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:18.421
'Cause if your worst enemy puts sugar

00:07:18.421 --> 00:07:20.059
in your coffee here, you're fine.

00:07:20.059 --> 00:07:22.273
If your best friend, by
accident, trying to help you,

00:07:22.273 --> 00:07:23.870
puts some strychnine in, you're dead.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.100
So, if you feed your mind
everyday, 30 minutes a day

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.456
of reading something, hearing something.

00:07:27.456 --> 00:07:29.388
Second, you got to strengthen your body.

00:07:29.388 --> 00:07:32.912
And the reason, Piers,
is fear is physical.

00:07:32.912 --> 00:07:37.481
So is stagnation, so is numbness,
so is sadness, so is rage,

00:07:37.481 --> 00:07:39.017
and when you go in to change your body

00:07:39.017 --> 00:07:41.777
by an intense workout or
run, or even an intense walk,

00:07:41.777 --> 00:07:43.134
and the blood's flowing through you,

00:07:43.134 --> 00:07:45.484
science has shown, it instantly
changes your biochemistry,

00:07:45.484 --> 00:07:47.315
and now your mind and
body are working together.

00:07:47.315 --> 00:07:49.205
Third thing, all these people
have in common if you watch,

00:07:49.205 --> 00:07:50.765
they've found a mission
bigger than themselves.

00:07:50.765 --> 00:07:53.745
Something that they want to aspire to

00:07:53.745 --> 00:07:55.835
that was worth more than their pain.

00:07:55.835 --> 00:07:56.946
And then the fourth thing is,

00:07:56.946 --> 00:07:58.105
you've got to find a role model.

00:07:58.105 --> 00:08:00.111
You know, you heard it with Nick.

00:08:00.111 --> 00:08:02.111
Almost everybody finds a role
model that makes it real.

00:08:02.111 --> 00:08:04.432
I was with Warren Buffet
and with Sarah Blakely,

00:08:04.432 --> 00:08:06.433
the youngest billionaire, we
were doing this round table

00:08:06.433 --> 00:08:08.642
about the future, and when
you listen to this woman,

00:08:08.642 --> 00:08:11.080
and when women meet her,
they don't just love Spanks,

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.475
her product that made her a billionaire.

00:08:12.475 --> 00:08:14.452
They love this woman
because she is a role model

00:08:14.452 --> 00:08:15.474
of what's possible.

00:08:15.474 --> 00:08:17.546
You get a role model,
it becomes real to you,

00:08:17.546 --> 00:08:19.866
if you get a plan, you get a goal plan,

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:20.864
and you take massive action.

00:08:20.864 --> 00:08:22.940
And the last step, number five,

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.892
there's always somebody
worse off than you are.

00:08:24.892 --> 00:08:26.030
I don't care what you've done.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.061
So if you can go help somebody worse off,

00:08:28.061 --> 00:08:29.665
it puts your life in perspective

00:08:29.665 --> 00:08:31.763
and it also reminds you
that life's not about me,

00:08:31.763 --> 00:08:32.596
it's about we.

00:08:32.596 --> 00:08:34.901
I always tell people, the
secret to a great life,

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:37.266
the secret to living, is giving.

00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:39.240
When you realize that there's
something still to give,

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.211
even if you lost your legs,

00:08:40.211 --> 00:08:42.647
even if you've been through a
horrific financial situation,

00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:44.049
your life can improve

00:08:44.049 --> 00:08:45.783
but more importantly you'll
have a meaningful life

00:08:45.783 --> 00:08:47.803
because your life will
contribute to other people.

00:08:47.803 --> 00:08:50.434
- There's a ton of bad
days being an entrepreneur.

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:52.565
Not to mention 98% of
entrepreneur adventures

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:55.377
are going to fail, so there's
going to be a really bad day

00:08:55.377 --> 00:08:56.557
in your future.

00:08:56.557 --> 00:08:58.092
(crowd laughs)

00:08:58.092 --> 00:09:02.009
You know, hopefully not
for you, or any of you.

00:09:02.849 --> 00:09:05.973
For me, I think this is
a very personal question,

00:09:05.973 --> 00:09:07.830
I think it's how you're wired.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.663
I'm so all in entrepreneur,
I prefer the pain.

00:09:11.663 --> 00:09:13.208
I think one of the reasons
I love the Jets so much

00:09:13.208 --> 00:09:15.007
is because they bring me so much pain.

00:09:15.007 --> 00:09:16.835
(crowd laughs)

00:09:16.835 --> 00:09:18.829
I love the climb.

00:09:18.829 --> 00:09:21.775
To me, the setback is exciting.

00:09:21.775 --> 00:09:23.993
I love when something goes wrong.

00:09:23.993 --> 00:09:26.141
It's where I shine the most.

00:09:26.141 --> 00:09:27.982
But that's not for everybody, right?

00:09:27.982 --> 00:09:29.616
I mean, it can be very difficult,

00:09:29.616 --> 00:09:31.298
and when you start affecting your life

00:09:31.298 --> 00:09:33.402
and your loved ones and
all the other things,

00:09:33.402 --> 00:09:35.270
it can get real nasty.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:38.972
To me, the way I handle things
even in the few rare days

00:09:38.972 --> 00:09:42.443
when I really struggle,
I take a real step back

00:09:42.443 --> 00:09:44.594
and make pretend that
somebody called me and told me

00:09:44.594 --> 00:09:47.829
that my mother or daughter were killed.

00:09:47.829 --> 00:09:50.926
And I know it's very
dark, and I apologize,

00:09:50.926 --> 00:09:52.071
but it's really what I do.

00:09:52.071 --> 00:09:55.863
I literally am able to, at my
deepest most struggling moment

00:09:55.863 --> 00:09:58.637
within business, take a step back

00:09:58.637 --> 00:10:00.372
and remind myself that I can make

00:10:00.372 --> 00:10:03.427
a trillion dollars tomorrow on Bitcoin,

00:10:03.427 --> 00:10:07.532
and if something bad happened
to the people I love the most,

00:10:07.532 --> 00:10:08.607
then it would mean nothing.

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:12.690
And it very consistently
rewires me very quickly.

00:10:13.569 --> 00:10:15.903
I just put business in perspective.

00:10:15.903 --> 00:10:19.171
At the end of the day, it's money.

00:10:19.171 --> 00:10:20.865
For me, it's not really
money, it's my legacy

00:10:20.865 --> 00:10:23.614
so I get hurt by it a little bit more,

00:10:23.614 --> 00:10:27.447
but yeah, I put it in
perspective, it's money.

00:10:28.462 --> 00:10:29.455
And you know what?

00:10:29.455 --> 00:10:32.051
Up until I had a daughter,
even while I was married,

00:10:32.051 --> 00:10:35.173
up until when I had Miesha four years ago,

00:10:35.173 --> 00:10:38.099
I secretly wanted to lose all my money.

00:10:38.099 --> 00:10:42.150
I had this weird, twisted, dark fantasy

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.810
of losing everything just to
rise again like a phoenix,

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.322
and remind you mother.

00:10:47.322 --> 00:10:49.905
(crowd laughs)

