00:11:23.574 --> 00:11:27.741
Much love, have an amazing
day, and I'll see you soon.

00:11:33.445 --> 00:11:34.716
Close your eyes and breathe.

00:11:34.716 --> 00:11:36.550
This sounds like a pretty basic one,

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:40.889
but just reminding yourself
that, this is stressful,

00:11:40.889 --> 00:11:45.164
I'm going to breathe, I'm going to
close my eyes, I'm going to relax,

00:11:45.164 --> 00:11:46.829
and things start to get better.

00:11:46.829 --> 00:11:49.462
Why do people go outside for a smoke?

00:11:49.462 --> 00:11:53.031
Like, the nicotine helps
but it's also the breathing,

00:11:53.031 --> 00:11:55.717
and so if there's a
reminder on your calendar

00:11:55.717 --> 00:11:58.312
or something on your desktop background,

00:11:58.312 --> 00:12:00.556
or whenever you feel that
stress coming on board,

00:12:00.556 --> 00:12:03.307
just reminding yourself,
I'm going to close my eyes.

00:12:03.307 --> 00:12:05.400
(inhales)

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.825
I'm going to take a couple deep breaths.

00:12:06.825 --> 00:12:07.977
(exhales)

00:12:07.977 --> 00:12:10.174
I'm going to instantly feel
a little bit more calm.

00:12:10.174 --> 00:12:13.792
- Anxiety usually is just
coming from three places,

00:12:13.792 --> 00:12:16.713
and once you realize it,
it's not so scary anymore.

00:12:16.713 --> 00:12:17.984
The scary part about anxiety

00:12:17.984 --> 00:12:19.824
is when you don't know why you have it.

00:12:19.824 --> 00:12:20.866
And again, for some people,

00:12:20.866 --> 00:12:22.623
they might have a chemical imbalance,

00:12:22.623 --> 00:12:24.563
they might have a challenge

00:12:24.563 --> 00:12:27.071
or a past unconscious traumatic event

00:12:27.071 --> 00:12:28.235
that is coming up for them,

00:12:28.235 --> 00:12:30.470
and they might need to seek some help for.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.585
Others can just sit down and go,

00:12:31.585 --> 00:12:33.420
"Okay, where is this coming from?"

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.640
And knowing that it's probably
coming from three places,

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:36.950
then now we can deal with it.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.646
Most anxiety comes from fear of loss.

00:12:39.646 --> 00:12:42.914
You feel like, in any uncertain situation,

00:12:42.914 --> 00:12:45.698
you feel like, "Gosh,
if I don't do well here,

00:12:45.698 --> 00:12:49.531
"I might lose reputation,
I might lose my job.

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.452
"I might lose someone's
respect or somebody's love.

00:12:53.452 --> 00:12:54.893
"I might lose something I like

00:12:54.893 --> 00:12:57.596
if I try something new
and it doesn't go well."

00:12:57.596 --> 00:12:59.391
It's just scared they
might lose something.

00:12:59.391 --> 00:13:00.969
So ask yourself next
time you feel anxiety,

00:13:00.969 --> 00:13:03.733
"What am I scared I'm going to lose here?

00:13:03.733 --> 00:13:06.100
"What could I be scared of
that I'm going to lose here?

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.575
"Maybe that's what I needed."

00:13:07.575 --> 00:13:10.112
And then, do fact checking, saying,

00:13:10.112 --> 00:13:11.817
"Is that legitimate?

00:13:11.817 --> 00:13:13.704
"Is that a concern that
I'm blowing up in my mind,

00:13:13.704 --> 00:13:16.489
"that I have no basis in
reality to figure out,

00:13:16.489 --> 00:13:19.233
"and if I don't, I need
to stop thinking about it

00:13:19.233 --> 00:13:20.716
"and I need to start focusing on

00:13:20.716 --> 00:13:24.834
"what's tangible action items
I can do tomorrow, or today,

00:13:24.834 --> 00:13:26.961
"to take one little tiny step closer."

00:13:26.961 --> 00:13:30.099
Because sometimes the easiest
way to wipe out anxiety

00:13:30.099 --> 00:13:32.909
is to get a little momentum.

00:13:32.909 --> 00:13:33.742
I would say the second thing

00:13:33.742 --> 00:13:36.659
that people often fear is hardship.

00:13:37.771 --> 00:13:39.970
They just think, the real anxiety is,

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:42.131
"I'm not going to be able to handle this.

00:13:42.131 --> 00:13:45.078
"I'm not enough as a person,
I don't have the skills,

00:13:45.078 --> 00:13:47.806
"the capabilities, the
competencies, the talent.

00:13:47.806 --> 00:13:51.023
"And if I try it, it's
going to be hard on me."

00:13:51.023 --> 00:13:52.884
People say, "It's going
to be too hard on me."

00:13:52.884 --> 00:13:53.983
And I tell people all the time,

00:13:53.983 --> 00:13:55.451
if that's coming from that...

00:13:55.451 --> 00:13:59.618
You have no idea how strong
of a human being you can be.

00:14:00.685 --> 00:14:01.965
You really don't, I don't.

00:14:01.965 --> 00:14:03.721
And I'm not saying that,
I'm not preaching here.

00:14:03.721 --> 00:14:06.076
I don't, we don't know.

00:14:06.076 --> 00:14:08.994
I'm stunned at the
things I can handle today

00:14:08.994 --> 00:14:11.156
that I couldn't handle 10 years ago.

00:14:11.156 --> 00:14:13.667
And I know there's areas
of your life like that too,

00:14:13.667 --> 00:14:15.852
things that you can just handle today.

00:14:15.852 --> 00:14:17.451
When you first tie your shoe,

00:14:17.451 --> 00:14:19.092
you fear that you're not going to be able

00:14:19.092 --> 00:14:20.209
to figure it out the next time,

00:14:20.209 --> 00:14:22.752
it's going to be too hard or
you're going to be embarrassed,

00:14:22.752 --> 00:14:25.484
but then you do it 10 times
and now you've got this,

00:14:25.484 --> 00:14:27.467
the hardship thing doesn't
bother you anymore.

00:14:27.467 --> 00:14:29.692
So one way to overcome
anxiety is to question,

00:14:29.692 --> 00:14:32.949
"Where do I feel like I'm not
going to enough or capable here?"

00:14:32.949 --> 00:14:34.894
And then start a little diagnosis and say,

00:14:34.894 --> 00:14:37.292
"But where have I been so capable before?

00:14:37.292 --> 00:14:39.225
"Or how could I develop this capability?

00:14:39.225 --> 00:14:41.192
"What support or mentorship could I get

00:14:41.192 --> 00:14:42.784
"to go to the next level here?

00:14:42.784 --> 00:14:45.313
"To know that I'm not going to
have to handle it on my own,

00:14:45.313 --> 00:14:46.943
"that I'll have real support."

00:14:46.943 --> 00:14:49.705
Because sometimes what we need
to know to overcome anxiety

00:14:49.705 --> 00:14:51.223
is that we'll be supported.

00:14:51.223 --> 00:14:53.502
Last piece I think
people really have a lot

00:14:53.502 --> 00:14:56.639
of anxiety towards is disappointment.

00:14:56.639 --> 00:14:59.271
They fear that they're
going to, they could do it,

00:14:59.271 --> 00:15:01.930
they could try, but maybe
it doesn't turn out well.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.405
And because it doesn't turn out well,

00:15:03.405 --> 00:15:05.675
they start inventing
all these reasons now.

00:15:05.675 --> 00:15:07.052
It's not going to turn out well,

00:15:07.052 --> 00:15:08.084
they're going to lose something,

00:15:08.084 --> 00:15:09.508
and they're going to have hardship,

00:15:09.508 --> 00:15:10.984
and they're going to feel like crap,

00:15:10.984 --> 00:15:11.964
(laughs) you know?

00:15:11.964 --> 00:15:16.744
They actually are fearing what
they're going to be feeling

00:15:16.744 --> 00:15:18.353
and that's the anxiety.

00:15:18.353 --> 00:15:20.027
The anxiety is actually just the sense of,

00:15:20.027 --> 00:15:21.805
"Oh my gosh, I might not feel good."

00:15:21.805 --> 00:15:25.422
And it causes us to feel even
worse, right, disappointment.

00:15:25.422 --> 00:15:27.668
And so you have to look at it and say,

00:15:27.668 --> 00:15:31.153
"Maybe I need to change my
value to criteria here."

00:15:31.153 --> 00:15:34.243
"Maybe this isn't about
whether or not I succeed.

00:15:34.243 --> 00:15:35.876
"Maybe it's about whether or not

00:15:35.876 --> 00:15:39.085
"I give effort towards something
that's meaningful to me.

00:15:39.085 --> 00:15:42.302
"Maybe it's not towards
whether it turns out perfect,

00:15:42.302 --> 00:15:44.662
"but it's that I began the journey."

00:15:44.662 --> 00:15:45.516
That we stop thinking about,

00:15:45.516 --> 00:15:47.965
is the destination going to be
perfect in the promised land

00:15:47.965 --> 00:15:50.642
for us, and instead we
ask this question is,

00:15:50.642 --> 00:15:52.476
can I develop as a human?

00:15:52.476 --> 00:15:54.260
Can I just, you know what, yes.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.279
Maybe part of me overcoming anxiety

00:15:56.279 --> 00:15:59.516
is getting more comfortable
with the uncomfortable.

00:15:59.516 --> 00:16:01.443
Not to get rid of the anxiety

00:16:01.443 --> 00:16:04.459
but to get rid of how I'm
dealing with the anxiety.

00:16:04.459 --> 00:16:08.045
To take pride in the
fact that, I'm facing it.

00:16:08.045 --> 00:16:10.703
I'm dealing with it, and
I'm still marching on.

00:16:10.703 --> 00:16:13.025
And I think if we face
it, we deal with it,

00:16:13.025 --> 00:16:14.482
and we still march on, we start

00:16:14.482 --> 00:16:17.649
to really start managing that anxiety.

00:16:18.527 --> 00:16:21.408
You have greater strength in your ability

00:16:21.408 --> 00:16:23.769
and in your body than you
could ever possibly imagine,

00:16:23.769 --> 00:16:25.136
and I'll say it all day long

00:16:25.136 --> 00:16:26.825
'cause you probably don't believe it

00:16:26.825 --> 00:16:30.276
in those moments when
you're experiencing anxiety.

00:16:30.276 --> 00:16:31.899
But next time you start
to experience anxiety,

00:16:31.899 --> 00:16:33.737
sit down and say,
"Where's this coming from?

00:16:33.737 --> 00:16:34.919
"Am I scared I'm going to lose something?

00:16:34.919 --> 00:16:36.039
"Am I scared of hardship?

00:16:36.039 --> 00:16:37.314
"Am I scared I'm going to be disappointed?

00:16:37.314 --> 00:16:41.040
"Do any of those things have
any factual matter to them?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.764
"And if they do, what am I
going to do with that energy?

00:16:43.764 --> 00:16:45.618
"Am I going to let it stop me,

00:16:45.618 --> 00:16:46.698
"or am I going to use it as a tool

00:16:46.698 --> 00:16:48.370
"to pay a little bit more attention,

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:49.636
"and to keep momentum because I know,

00:16:49.636 --> 00:16:52.415
"the more momentum I get
the less anxiety I'll have."

00:16:52.415 --> 00:16:54.012
Start focusing on
developing your strengths

00:16:54.012 --> 00:16:55.961
and your momentum, and
you'll start to experience

00:16:55.961 --> 00:16:58.454
what we call the charged life.

00:16:58.454 --> 00:17:01.480
- Worry beads, this is not philosophical.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.129
Don't worry about the, you know,

00:17:04.129 --> 00:17:07.064
this is a really practical tactic.

00:17:07.064 --> 00:17:11.408
Get a bunch of beads or
beans or whatever it is,

00:17:11.408 --> 00:17:13.334
and every time you're at your desk working

00:17:13.334 --> 00:17:15.865
and your mind goes to a worry,

00:17:15.865 --> 00:17:18.615
dump one of those beads or beans,

00:17:19.489 --> 00:17:22.054
a dried bean, I'm sure you can get them.

00:17:22.054 --> 00:17:23.595
Don't make any excuses, don't say,

00:17:23.595 --> 00:17:26.064
"Well I don't live in a city
where I can get worry beads."

00:17:26.064 --> 00:17:29.226
You can find some kind of bean or a bead.

00:17:29.226 --> 00:17:31.500
Isn't it interesting
how worries prevent us

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:32.408
from taking action?

00:17:32.408 --> 00:17:35.568
Excuses prevent us from taking action.

00:17:35.568 --> 00:17:36.989
And so on this second point you just,

00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:39.486
every time your mind drifts to a worry,

00:17:39.486 --> 00:17:42.750
you drop the worry bead
into a cup or into a glass.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:43.692
What does that do?

00:17:43.692 --> 00:17:46.233
It starts to give you an intense awareness

00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:48.663
about how much time you spend worrying,

00:17:48.663 --> 00:17:52.176
and more particularly,
how many worries you have.

00:17:52.176 --> 00:17:55.536
And with more awareness,
you can make better choices.

00:17:55.536 --> 00:17:57.766
And with better choices,
you'll see better results.

00:17:57.766 --> 00:17:58.599
Okay.

